 **Parameters:**
-*   **Enable lighting:** Boolean flag to enable lighting calculations (e.g., Phong model) [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Enable early ray termination:** Boolean optimization flag. Note: Sources state this requires lighting to be disabled [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Enable cubic interpolation:** Boolean flag to use cubic interpolation for the 3D volume texture and gradient texture [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Trapezoid Slope:** The slope of the trapezoidal transfer function can be adjusted to include more structures with lower attenuation (sliding towards lower Hounsfield units) or fewer (sliding towards higher values) [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Sample Distance:** Controls the step size along the ray. Typical values are 0.5, 1.0, 2.0, or 4.0. Lower values increase quality but decrease performance [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Enable Lighting:** Boolean flag. If true, lighting calculations are performed. Note: Early ray termination must be disabled if lighting is enabled [S2, unofficial].
+*   **Enable Early Ray Termination:** Boolean flag. Stops ray casting when accumulated opacity exceeds a threshold. Requires lighting to be disabled [S2, unofficial].
+*   **Enable Cubic Interpolation:** Boolean flag. Uses cubic interpolation for volume and gradient textures instead of linear [S2, unofficial].
 
 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Opacity Transfer Function Changes:** The opacity transfer function must not change after precomputation because the voxel opacities are fixed in the preclassified volume [S4]. If the transfer function changes, `vpRenderRawVolume` (with an octree) should be used instead [S4].
-*   **Anatomical Masking:** VR can mask anatomical information and pathology. For example, in intracranial aneurysm visualization, bone subtraction is often required to avoid missing critical information [S3, unofficial].
-*   **Precomputation Time:** Precomputing the run-length encoded volume can take several minutes, making it unsuitable for interactive transfer function tuning [S2].
+*   **Opacity Transfer Function Stability:** The opacity transfer function must not change between precomputation and rendering. If it changes, the pre-classified volume becomes invalid, and the precomputation step must be repeated [S5].
+*   **Masking Pathology:** Classified VR can mask anatomical information. For example, in intracranial aneurysm visualization, bone subtraction is often required because the bone classification may obscure critical details [S4, unofficial].
+*   **Precomputation Time:** The initial classification step can take several minutes, making this method unsuitable for interactive classification adjustment [S3].
 
